{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:9-3","provision":"BCO 9-3","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"9-3","title":"Section 9-3","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/9-3/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/9-3","current_text":{"html":"<p>To the office of deacon, which is spiritual in nature, shall be chosen men of spiritual character, honest repute, exemplary lives, brotherly spirit, warm sympathies, and sound judgment, conforming to the biblical requirement of chastity and sexual purity in their descriptions of themselves and in their convictions, character, and conduct.</p>","text":"To the office of deacon, which is spiritual in nature, shall be chosen men of spiritual character, honest repute, exemplary lives, brotherly spirit, warm sympathies, and sound judgment, conforming to the biblical requirement of chastity and sexual purity in their descriptions of themselves and in their convictions, character, and conduct."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"f8bde72b35f9475713a5751081d525f119bc6b4daf3b43ddc86694065015654b","parent_id":"bco:9","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":17,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:9-3--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga50_2023__ci16.md","record_id":"ccb_advice:inquiries/ga50_2023__ci16.md","type":"CCB advice","title":"Officers required to conform to biblical chastity in self-description","year":2023,"disposition":"not in conflict; Adopted 8-0-0","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga50_2023__ci16.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga50_2023__ci16.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga50_2023__ci16.md:occ-d7a0536609ba","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga50_2023__ci16.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga50_2023__ci16.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"The CCB found that amending BCO 8-2 and 9-3 to require officers to conform to biblical standards of chastity and sexual purity in self-description is not in conflict with the BCO.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga50_2023__ci16.md"}]},{"id":"bco:9-3--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.md","record_id":"ccb_advice:inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.md","type":"CCB advice","title":"5-9.i(1)","year":2019,"disposition":"not in conflict; Adopted by the CCB","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.md:occ-c93fa1d1e6ab","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"This overture proposed amending multiple BCO provisions to allow individual sessions to decide locally whether women may serve as deacons; the CCB found it not in conflict.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga47_2019__ci17.md"}]},{"id":"bco:9-3--inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Ordination of men who believe women may serve as deacons","year":1984,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.md:occ-436a36dac79a","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"Believing Scripture permits women deacons, while agreeing to abide by BCO standards in practice, is not by itself sufficient grounds to deny ordination or reception in the PCA.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci09.md"}]},{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Crouse v. Northwest Georgia Presbytery","year":2021,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.md:occ-85665b91c72c","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":135},"excerpt":"In this case, the Session of Midway Presbyterian Church had a Constitutional duty to report candidates that were <u>eligible for election</u> to the congregation. (BCO 24-1). While there is no one place in the Constitution of the Church that defines “eligible ","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga48_2021__2019-11.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["deacon re-election","eligibility for office","session discretion","de facto deposition","retaliation for complaint","standard of review","BCO 39-3 deference","right to file complaint","officer nomination","candidate eligibility"],"standard_of_review":"discretion_and_judgment","review_standards":["discretion_and_judgment"],"case_numbers":["2019-11"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"A complaint challenging a session's refusal to advance an ordained deacon's nomination for re-election to the diaconate was denied by the SJC. Northwest Georgia Presbytery had adopted its judicial commission's judgment that the session did not err; applying BCO 39-3(3)'s deference to discretionary judgments, the SJC found no clear error, held formal charges were unnecessary and re-election was not guaranteed, and refused to attribute one elder's questionable retaliation rationale to the session. The majority encouraged prompt communication of reasons. A dissent would apply BCO 39-3.4 and sustain."}},{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Brown v. Northern California Presbytery","year":2011,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md:occ-acfca64a6847","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","repository_path":"cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":380},"excerpt":"This difference between Grasso and the NORD view also applies to the exception cited by two General Assemblies to Northern California's Minutes. The 35th GA cited Presbytery with an exception of substance in their Minutes of March 2006, describing the exceptio","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md"},{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md:occ-06c3ad8677e3","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","repository_path":"cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":382},"excerpt":"> “The newly installed Session of the particularized Church “commissioned\" unordained men and women for a body which the Presbytery minutes called the “diaconate\" (BCO 9, 19-15, 24-10). However, BCO 9 is clear that only ordained and elected men can be Members ","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["diaconate","deaconess","women in church office","in thesi statement","abstract decree","presbyterial jurisdiction","BCO 9-7","appointed deaconess","elected deaconess","equal partners","nobody ordained","GUMP standard","Kniseley standard"],"standard_of_review":"constitutional_interpretation","review_standards":["constitutional_interpretation"],"case_numbers":["2009-26"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Joined with Case 2009-25; the Session of Grace Presbyterian Church complained that views 3, 4, 5, and 6 in Northern California Presbytery's resolution on diaconal practice violated the BCO. The SJC sustained the complaint on the same grounds as 2009-25, annulling the abstract resolution while declining to rule on the constitutional merits of any specific diaconal view."}},{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"David Kniseley et al. v. Rocky Mountain Presbytery","year":2009,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md:occ-383e7d744566","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["minister title","non-ordained staff","women","constitutional interpretation","presbytery judgment"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2007-13"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"On complaint from TE David Kniseley and others, the SJC reviewed Rocky Mountain Presbytery's refusal to forbid a mission church from giving an unordained female staff member the title 'Minister of Church Life.' The SJC denied the complaint. It held the BCO uses 'minister' synonymously with pastor and teaching elder, but is silent on general use for non-ordained staff; a lower court may exercise discretion subject to BCO 40-2(3)'s WESP review. The decision addressed only the constitutional issue, not the title's wisdom or propriety; four commissioners dissented."}},{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Session of Crossroads Community Church v. Philadelphia Presbytery","year":2009,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md:occ-7405b55fd9a6","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["ordination","licensure","women deacons","stated difference","confessional subscription"],"standard_of_review":"discretion_and_judgment","review_standards":["discretion_and_judgment"],"case_numbers":["2008-1"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The Session of Crossroads Community Church challenged Philadelphia Presbytery's licensing and ordination of a candidate who stated a difference concerning women and the office of deacon but agreed to follow the BCO. The SJC denied the complaint and affirmed Presbytery's judgment; a dissent argued it should have been sustained."}},{"id":"bco:9-3--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/chesapeake__011.html","record_id":"rpr_exception:rpr/exc/chesapeake__011.html","type":"RPR exception","title":"Chesapeake: A session was improperly granted four years to come to compliance with BCO 7-2 and 9-3.","year":2014,"disposition":"unsatisfactory","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/chesapeake__011.html","raw_